      "section_title": "Grafting a List",
      "section_number": 3,
      "teaching_text": "3- Grafting a List:\r\n\r\n- \"Grafting\" a List makes each of the items a Branch!\r\n\r\n- So in a way, it does the opposite of what \"Flatenning\" does.\r\n\r\n- Type \"Graft\" and graft the flatenned tree.\r\n\r\n- Notice that as there used to be 10 items inside the flatenned List, after grafting the List, there are now 10 Branches inside this new Tree!\r\n\r\n- There is also the \"Unflatten Tree\" which unflattens a Tree using a path guide. This component is not often used.",
      "teaching_panel_id": "C386",
      "additional_teaching_panels": [],
